{{!
    @template tool_vae/booklet_authorize_form

    The button that authorizes a manager to produce the archive of the structure, or takes the authorization back: a form
    that posts the session key, the manager and the action. Its elements stand side by side with no space between them (a
    comment carries each line break of the template, so that no space is drawn).

    Every value comes from the context, given by tool_vae\output\booklet_authorize_form. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - string, the address of the page, not escaped
    * sesskey - string, the session key
    * managerid - int, the manager
    * verb - string, the action: grant or revoke
    * label - string, the words of the button

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/booklet_authorize.php",
        "sesskey": "abcdef1234",
        "managerid": 4,
        "verb": "grant",
        "label": "Authorize"
    }
}}
<form method="post" action="{{url}}" class="d-inline">{{!
}}<input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">{{!
}}<input type="hidden" name="managerid" value="{{managerid}}">{{!
}}<input type="hidden" name="action" value="{{verb}}">{{!
}}<button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">{{label}}</button>{{!
}}</form>
